---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = 'August 20, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${site.name}`}
  description="How Professional Construction LLC collects, uses, and protects the information you share when you request a free estimate."
>
  <section class="policy">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      </header>

      <div class="body">
        <p class="lede">
          {site.name} (&ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) respects your
          privacy. This policy explains what information we collect when you contact us or request
          a free estimate, how we use it, and the choices you have.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          {site.name} is a licensed roofing and general construction contractor based in {site.city},
          serving {site.serviceArea}. You can reach us at
          <a href={`tel:${site.phoneRaw}`}>{site.phone}</a> or
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
        <p>We only collect information you choose to give us. That usually means:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact details</strong> — your name, phone number, and email address.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Property details</strong> — the address of the property, the approximate age of
            the roof, and what you need done. We need the address to schedule an inspection and
            price the work.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Photos and notes</strong> — any images or descriptions you send us about the
            condition of your roof or property.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>We collect this through:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The contact form on this website.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Lead forms on Facebook and Instagram.</strong> When you submit one of our ads on
            Meta platforms, Meta passes us the information you confirmed in that form. Meta&rsquo;s
            own handling of your data is governed by the
            <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Meta Privacy Policy</a>.
          </li>
          <li>Phone calls, text messages, and WhatsApp conversations you start with us.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18, and we do not ask for Social
          Security numbers, bank account numbers, or payment card numbers through any online form.
        </p>

        <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
        <p>We use what you give us to do the job you asked us to do:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Contact you to schedule a free roof inspection or estimate.</li>
          <li>Prepare and send you a written scope of work and pricing.</li>
          <li>Answer your questions and follow up on work in progress.</li>
          <li>Keep records of completed projects and warranty coverage.</li>
          <li>Meet legal, permitting, and insurance obligations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Calls, texts, and messages</h2>
        <p>
          When you submit a form or send us a message, you agree that we may contact you by phone
          call, text message, email, or WhatsApp at the contact details you provided, including
          about your estimate and scheduling. Message and data rates may apply. You can stop
          receiving messages at any time by replying <strong>STOP</strong> or by telling us directly
          — it will not affect any work already underway. We do not send marketing blasts.
        </p>

        <h2>5. How we share information</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not rent or trade it to
          advertisers or lead brokers.</strong> We share it only when necessary:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>With people who work on your project</strong> — our crew, and where relevant
            suppliers or subcontractors who need the address to deliver materials or perform work.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>With service providers</strong> that help us run the business, such as our
            website host and email provider, and only to the extent they need it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>With your insurance company</strong>, if you ask us to assist with a claim.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>When the law requires it</strong> — for permits, inspections, a subpoena, or a
            valid legal request.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          If you request an estimate and do not hire us, we keep your information for up to two
          years and then delete it. If we complete work for you, we keep project records for the
          length of the applicable workmanship warranty plus any period required by law, since we
          need them to honor warranty claims.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your choices</h2>
        <p>You can ask us at any time to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Tell you what information we hold about you.</li>
          <li>Correct anything that is wrong.</li>
          <li>Delete your information, unless we are required to keep it for warranty or legal reasons.</li>
          <li>Stop contacting you.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call
          <a href={`tel:${site.phoneRaw}`}>{site.phone}</a> and we will take care of it. We aim to
          respond within 30 days. We will not treat you differently for making a request.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Cookies and website analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This site uses only what it needs to load pages and deliver your form submission. We do
          not use cookies to build advertising profiles on this website. If you reached us from an
          ad on Facebook or Instagram, Meta may record that interaction on its own platform under
          its policy, not ours.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Security</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable steps to protect the information you send us. No method of transmission
          over the internet is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security — but we
          limit who can see your details to the people who need them for your project.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change how we handle information, we will update this page and change the date at
          the top. Material changes will be reflected here before they take effect.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy, or about information we hold?
        </p>
        <ul class="contact-list">
          <li><strong>{site.name}</strong></li>
          <li>{site.city} &middot; Serving {site.serviceArea}</li>
          <li><a href={`tel:${site.phoneRaw}`}>{site.phone}</a></li>
          <li><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy {
    padding: 4.5rem 0 6rem;
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .head {
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-primary-dark);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .body :global(h2) {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-primary-dark);
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.85rem;
  }

  .body :global(p) {
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .body :global(ul) {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  .body :global(li) {
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .body :global(a) {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .body :global(a:hover) {
    color: var(--color-accent-dark);
  }

  .contact-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin-left: 0 !important;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }
</style>
